For the sake of this dinner party, I'll choose some historical figures that have significantly shaped human understanding and achievement:

1. Galileo Galilei - the Italian astronomer who made fundamental contributions to the science of optics and invented the telescope;
2. Isaac Newton - the English mathematician and physicist (though he is known as "Isaac" rather than "Sir" nowadays) who formulated the law of universal gravitation;
3. Alexander Graham Bell - the Scottish-born inventor of the telephone, dedicated to improving communication technologies;
4. Charles Babbage - the English mathematician who is often called the father of computing;
5. Ada Lovelace - the world's first programmer.

