Certainly! I'd be delighted to host a dinner party for the following set of historical figures:

1. Socrates - the ancient Greek philosopher who made important contributions to Western philosophy;
2. Leonardo da Vinci - an Italian inventor and artist who painted masterpieces like the Mona Lisa;
3. Archimedes - an ancient Greek mathematician who invented the Archimedean screw;
4. Ada Lovelace - the daughter of famous inventor Charles Babbage who worked on his analytical engine and later married him;
5. Marie Curie - a physicist known for her work on radioactivity, alongside which she received a Nobel Prize in Physics;

